code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a matching with no edge (other than a self-loop) between two free vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"is_maximal_matching","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"title":"isMaximalMatching(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isMaximalMatching","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isMaximalMatching(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/ismaximalmatching(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumMatching()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumMatching()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum-cardinality matching by Edmonds’ blossom algorithm: for each still-free vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, a breadth-first alternating search (rows in "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order) that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contracts blossoms and augments along the first free vertex found, skipping the vertices of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier failed searches. The matching returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this procedure’s, a documented function of the vertex order and rows. Parallel edges: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy met first. Vertices of a search that fails are skipped by later se